/** \dir Grid/parallelIO
 * \anchor parallelIO
 * This directory contains implementations of
 * reading and writing lattice objects in common formats.
 *
 * Implementations include:
 *
 * - \ref binaryio_h "BinaryIO.h": Raw binary files
 * - IldgIO.h: The <a href="https://ildg.net">International %Lattice Data %Grid</a> standard format and related formats
 * - NerscIO.h: The <a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1112.2193.pdf">NERSC</a> format
 * - OpenQcdIO.h: The <a href="https://luscher.web.cern.ch/luscher/openQCD/">openQCD</a> format
 *
 * \section mungers Mungers and unmungers
 *
 * Some formats use a different matrix format on disk to that used by %Grid in memory.
 * For example,
 * ILDG allows storing a subset of the rows of a square unitary or symplecti matrix,
 * and reconstructing the missing ones when loading the file.
 *
 * In such cases,
 * \em munging refers to the reconstruction done when reading from disk
 * (reconstructing missing rows),
 * and \em unmunging refers to the preparation done for writing to disk
 * (dropping rows from the input data matrices).
 */
